Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/v4l2m2m: complete metadata and DRC boundaries before capture resume

Initialize CAPTURE only after the first source-change event. For later
source changes, consume the old CAPTURE LAST before START or rebuilding the
capture queue. Preserve actual old frames and keep an explicit EOF drain
separate from a source-change drain. Do not turn an empty LAST into a frame.

Keep buffer references alive until users release them. Account for one
context reference per buffer, and finish callback buffer access before
waking a capture remap. Initial input exhaustion without stream metadata
returns invalid data after all OUTPUT buffers and pending events are read.

Base: FFmpeg 7.1.5, Debian upstream archive SHA256
 de668509caf9e35e3cd162473441fdb29538c6d96ed080292b3cf9e6fc5d558f
This is a BSP prototype awaiting real stateful decoder validation.

